"_3\nWill ye come, and sail my Marion\nAll on the silver sea?\nFear not the waves my Marion,\nThou'rt safe, for thou'rt with me:\nThere's many a heart my Marion,\nThat now beats high for thee;\nThere's many sigh for Marion,\nBut none that loves like me." C,2 G,,2 | %86
